{
  "mn77:0.1": "Middle Discourses 77 ",
  "mn77:0.2": "The Longer Discourse with Sakuludāyī ",
  "mn77:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn77:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Rājagaha in the Bamboo Grove, the squirrels’ feeding ground. ",
  "mn77:2.1": "Now at that time several very well-known wanderers were residing in their monastery in the peacocks’ feeding ground. ",
  "mn77:2.2": "They included Annabhāra, Varadhara, Sakuludāyī, and other very well-known wanderers. ",
  "mn77:3.1": "Then the Buddha robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, entered Rājagaha for alms. ",
  "mn77:3.2": "Then it occurred to him, ",
  "mn77:3.3": "“It’s too early to wander for alms in Rājagaha. ",
  "mn77:3.4": "Why don’t I visit the wanderer Sakuludāyī at the monastery for the wanderers in the peacocks’ feeding ground?” ",
  "mn77:4.1": "So the Buddha went to the monastery for the wanderers. ",
  "mn77:4.2": "Now at that time, Sakuludāyī was sitting together with a large assembly of wanderers making an uproar, a colossal racket. They engaged in all kinds of low talk, such as ",
  "mn77:4.3": "talk about kings, bandits, and chief ministers; talk about armies, threats, and wars; talk about food, drink, clothes, and beds; talk about garlands and fragrances; talk about family, vehicles, villages, towns, cities, and countries; talk about women and heroes; talk at the street market and the place for water pots; talk about the departed; motley talk; tales of land and sea; and talk abou